<!--
  CLI Documentation — V1Scope
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.V1Scope
-->
<block
  xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://blockml.org/bml https://blockml.org/schemas/bml.xsd
                      "
  xmlns:blockml="org.blockml.bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:def="org.blockml.bml.definition"
  xmlns:cli="org.blockml.bml.cli"
  xmlns:cliapi="org.blockml.bml.cli.api"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clicommand="org.blockml.bml.cli.command"
  xmlns:cliconfig="org.blockml.bml.cli.config"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:runtime="org.blockml.bml.compiler.runtime"
  xmlns:framework="org.blockml.bml.framework"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:doc="org.blockml.bml.documentation">

  <name>V1Scope</name>
  <type>clidocumentation:V1Scope</type>
  <baseType>core:Documentation</baseType>
  <is>V1 implemented vs planned commands</is>

  <documentation>V1 implemented:
    • blockml validate [file] [--all] [--src] [--libraries] [--verbose]
      (default: project sources; --all: entire registry including npm)
    • blockml compile [file] target | blockml compile target
    • blockml search QUERY [--json] [--limit] [--src] [--libraries]
    • blockml search index [--force]
    • blockml graph index [--force]
    • blockml graph neighbors|uses|used-by|ancestors|descendants|members FQN [--json] [--depth]
    • blockml graph path FROM TO [--json] [--depth]
    • blockml graph query CYPHER [--json]
    • blockml graph schema [--json]
    • blockml inspect FQN [--depth n] [--json] [--src] [--libraries]
    • blockml transform apply EXECUTION-FQN [--library] [--verbose]
    • blockml new FQN [--baseType FQN] [--is text]
    • Targets: blockdoc (default), xsd, fatblock; custom via registerTargetFactory or targetPackages
    • Config: targets[], targetPackages, targetOptions, defaultTarget
    • Flags: --out, --src, --libraries, --library (transform apply target Library.bml), --include (fatblock), --per-package (fatblock), --all, --verbose (validate, transform), --json (search, graph, inspect), --limit (search), --force (search/graph index), --depth (graph, inspect), --baseType (new), --is (new)
    • Validate uses parse + @blockml/validator only; XSD is compile xsd, not a validate step
    • Search uses @blockml/search over the validate --all corpus
    • Graph uses @blockml/graph over the validate --all corpus
    • Inspect uses @blockml/inspect over the validate --all corpus
    • New uses @blockml/builder; writes .bml and updates Library.blocks

    V1 not implemented (documented in ScopeExclusions):
    init, watch, activate-config,
    incremental .bom-cache, thumbnails, OpenSCAD resolver, bom-cli.config.json renaming.</documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:PublicApi" relation="ReadNext" />
  </references>

</block>
